course: dictionary
lesson: 11490
title: Agenda and meetings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An agenda is a list of things to be talked about or done at a meeting. Think of it as the plan for the meeting, written in order. «The agenda for the school council has three items: lunch menu, playground and trips.» Each item is something the meeting will talk about.
explain: Agenda can also mean the things someone plans or wants to do. «What's on the agenda today?» means "What are we going to do today?" You can hear this in everyday talk, not just at meetings.
explain: Watch for the phrases. «On the agenda» means it will be discussed. «Top of the agenda» means the most important thing, to be talked about first. A «hidden agenda» is a secret aim: someone wants something but does not say so.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. If the sentence is about a meeting, a list or a plan, agenda probably means the list or plan. Check by swapping in "list of things to talk about" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Agenda is a noun, and its plural is agendas.
fact: «Agenda» means a list of things to be talked about or done at a meeting.
fact: «Agenda» can also mean things someone plans or wants to do.
fact: A «hidden agenda» is a secret aim or plan.
fact: «Set the agenda» means to decide what will be talked about or done first.
exercise: «The head teacher read out the agenda before the meeting started.» What is the agenda here? | A bag for carrying books | A game played in the playground | *A list of things to be talked about at the meeting | A type of school dinner
exercise: «Lunch menu is top of the agenda today.» What does top of the agenda mean? | The lunch menu is the last thing on the list | *The lunch menu is the most important thing to talk about first | The lunch menu is written at the top of the page | The lunch menu is served on a tray
exercise: Sam says he only wants to help, but he has a «hidden agenda». What does hidden agenda mean? | Something the whole class can see | *A secret aim or plan | A new game | A kind of pencil case
test: «What's on the agenda for the trip?» What does agenda mean here? | *Things someone plans or wants to do | A school report | A map of the town | A type of bus
test: Which word means a list of things to be talked about at a meeting? | Umbrella | Holiday | *Agenda | Canteen
exam: Maya says a «hidden agenda» is a hidden bag of agendas. Is she right? | Yes, it is a list of meetings | *No, a hidden agenda is a secret aim or plan | Yes, it is a type of pencil case | No, it is a game played at lunch
